  "id": "neural-representation",
  "term": "neural representation",
  "definition": "In this historical source, neural representation means the supposed pattern of combined activity or union among nerve-centres that stands for a thought in the brain. It is described as a preparatory neural arrangement, analogous to the way nerve-centres organize themselves before carrying out a coordinated movement.",
